.TH "PAIRDESK-REMOTE" "1" "November 2026" "PairDesk 2.9.2" "User Commands"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
pairdesk-remote - PairDesk\[cq]s side of a connection on the remote
computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]pairdesk-remote\f[R]
\f[B]serve\f[R]|\f[B]pair-gate\f[R]|\f[B]sockcat\f[R] \&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Not meant to be run by hand.
PairDesk\[cq]s link service runs it as the forced command of each paired
computer\[cq]s key, so that a key can only run the requests listed in
it: status, USB device sharing, shared folders, the desktop\[cq]s
certificate fingerprint, signing out the local session, unpairing, and
exchanging PairDesk updates (a received package is only kept; installing
it needs an administrator of that computer).
A computer that isn\[cq]t paired yet knocks with a fresh random key;
\f[B]pairdesk-knock\f[R] lets such a key in to \f[B]pair-gate\f[R] only,
which can only ask for a one-time pairing code to be shown, or pair with
that code (a code works only for the key that asked for it).
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\f[B]pairdesk\f[R](1)
